The collector reads a City-schema GeoIP database from here. The compose file
mounts this directory into it read-only.

Run `./fetch-dbip.sh` to download one. It fetches DB-IP City Lite, which is
CC BY 4.0 — no account, direct download, redistributable with attribution — and
prints the attribution line the licence requires. `generate-secrets.sh
--with-geoip` runs it for you and fills in GEOIP_DB_PATH.

MaxMind's GeoLite2-City.mmdb works equally well if you already have one: the
schemas are interchangeable. Drop it here and point GEOIP_DB_PATH at it. It
needs a MaxMind account and its licence forbids redistribution, which is why
nothing here fetches it.

No database is committed. Without one, every event carries null geo — a
degradation, never a failure.
